f 17592186045417] [17592186198532 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198532 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198532 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198532 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198532 #edb/ref 1045 "Visualizing Cartesian Products" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198532 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186199077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198532 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048206 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198532 #edb/ref 1050 720.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198532 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "da7c19c9-a092-5227-8c3d-c60c670a8222" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199077 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199077 #edb/ref 1061 153383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199077 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c7652427-e5ff-5d02-9f23-39039f090aff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199077 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199078 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199078 #edb/ref 1061 153384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199078 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2190f1df-5853-5d8c-85e2-33f40f1f0f24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199078 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199079 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199079 #edb/ref 1061 153387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199079 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cd371945-c79b-5b78-9017-15c39e4d5ed7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199079 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199080 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199080 #edb/ref 1061 153388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199080 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "48b1fb46-7071-5897-9dd7-a47e1d955f6c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199080 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199081 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199081 #edb/ref 1061 153392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199081 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ef01039c-9cce-558a-8067-2ffba087e848" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199081 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199082 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199082 #edb/ref 1061 153393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199082 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9ddfd97d-7a1a-59ef-8492-3fbe4088f22f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199082 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198274 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199083 #edb/ref 1061 153396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199083 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5777ec1b-f050-570f-86e4-1e7bffa77dfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199083 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198275 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199560 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that if $A$ and $B$ are sets, the Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs $(a,b)$ whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA \\times B = \\big\\{(a, b) \\: : \\: a \\in A,\\, b \\in B \\big\\}\n$$\n\nMany Cartesian products have natural representations in the Cartesian plane. The most common of these is the Cartesian product $\\mathbb R^2{:}$\n\n$$\n\\mathbb R^2 = \\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R =  \\big\\{(x, y) \\: : \\: x,y \\in \\mathbb R \\big\\}\n$$\n\nThis infinite set contains all ordered pairs $(x,y),$ where $x$ and $y$ can be any real numbers. In other words, $\\mathbb R^2$ contains every point in the Cartesian plane! \n\n![](images/07/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png)\n\nSimilarly, the set\n\n$$\n\\mathbb R^3 = \\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R =  \\big\\{(x, y, z) \\: : \\: x,y,z \\in \\mathbb R \\big\\}\n$$\n\ndescribes every point in three-dimensional Cartesian space. \n\n![](images/e7/e74fb5948144bc61173e4de73865cb746278bd31fd87e4abf927fa01821ba936.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199560 #edb/ref 1065 8237 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199560 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c18e6618-573b-5560-8d95-58ed56f05155" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199560 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199579 #edb/ref 1064 "Cartesian coordinates can also be used to visualize other Cartesian products.\n\nFor example, let's consider the following Cartesian product:\n\n$$\n\\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{R}^- = \\big\\{(x,y) \\: : \\: x\\in\\mathbb N,\\, y\\in\\mathbb R^-\\big\\}\n$$\n\nThis product contains every point in $\\mathbb R^2$ whose $x$-coordinate is a natural number and whose $y$-coordinate is a negative real number.\n\nTo visualize this Cartesian product, consider the following subset of our Cartesian product:\n\n$$\nS_1 = \\big\\{ (1,y) \\: : \\: y \\in\\mathbb{R}^- \\big\\} \\subset \\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{R}^-\n$$\n\nThis subset describes all points in the plane whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any negative real number. We can represent $S_1$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/f6/f6165f66b4149b7b2ea52a3cd686836853d85048ca890e850cb771174a150c57.png)\n\nNext, we consider the subset $S_2,$ given by\n\n$$\nS_2 = \\big\\{ (2,y) \\: : \\: y \\in\\mathbb{R}^- \\big\\} \\subset \\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{R}^-.\n$$\n\nThis subset describes all points in the plane whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any negative real number. \n\n![](images/ca/caf2299a2e8009ad5b2776ce67786fa7c7e3bdb57aacbd7df87882f59a2350e2.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $S_3, S_4, S_5,\\ldots,$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N\\times {R}^{-} & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup ⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $\\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{R}^-$ as the set of vertical rays shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/03/033c40b86bfd5cebf24d34de644f632213207386c2b67c559af7594468599e1e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199579 #edb/ref 1065 8329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199579 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1626e562-8e88-5ff3-bae3-4162438c0086" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199579 #edb/ref 1067 "Cartesian Products of Countably Infinite Sets" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199584 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's sketch a representation of the set $S= [0,1] \\times [0,1]$ in the Cartesian plane.\n\nThe Cartesian product $A \\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B = \\big\\{(a,b) \\::\\: a\\in A,\\, b\\in B\\big\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS = [0,1] \\times [0, 1]\n$$\n\ncontains every point in $\\mathbb{R}^2$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\nS=\n\\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: x\\in [0,1],\\, y\\in [0,1] \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider $S_0 \\subset S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals ${\\color{red}0}$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\nS_{\\color{red}0} = \\big\\{ ({\\color{red}{0}},y) \\: : \\: y \\in [0,1]\\big\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent $S_{\\color{red}0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/1c/1cc30fcc7543bfbbf8c5c59d1436eb3b1a0799d60c9ad1d899957e8fd17d58ab.png)\n\nNow, consider a general $S_{\\color{blue}{i}} \\subset S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some ${\\color{blue}{i}} \\in [0,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,1].$\n\n$$\nS_{\\color{blue}{i}} = \\big\\{ ({\\color{blue}{i}},y) \\: : \\: y \\in [0,1]\\big\\}\n$$\n\nFor each ${\\color{blue}{i}} \\in [0,1],$ $S_{\\color{blue}{i}}$ is a vertical line segment from the point $({\\color{blue}{i}},0)$ to the point $({\\color{blue}{i}},1).$\n\n![](images/28/28b9aa0559635ed4090f10dd0b59f2cbb6c297f8736d9509a637b5d78d27561c.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $I = [0,1]{:}$\n\n$$\nS = \\bigcup_{{\\color{blue}i} \\in I} S_{\\color{blue}i}.\n$$\n\nAs $\\color{blue}i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following rectangle that represents the union $\\displaystyle \\bigcup_{{\\color{blue}i} \\in I} S_{\\color{blue}i}{:}$\n\n![](images/76/76ff48755dbfc3ba1943665d08aa8cfd00948bbc1ddfaab560a0af64f11bae26.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199584 #edb/ref 1065 8339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199584 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "923fb377-d694-5181-8561-c57612f15054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199584 #edb/ref 1067 "The Cartesian Product [0,1] x [0,1]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236171 #edb/ref 1080 "x=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236171 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236171 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "37503db8-10d7-5583-8f30-374405d5c1fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236258 #edb/ref 1080 "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236258 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236258 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4461e345-3733-5f04-8b2d-ba7bcab3ab70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236501 #edb/ref 1080 "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236501 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236501 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6ca5d4f4-cb39-51c0-989f-7439bc2613f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236631 #edb/ref 1080 "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236631 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186236631 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "825b8a80-c42c-526f-8704-24d7b15a4dde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237317 #edb/ref 1080 "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237317 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237317 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee57336e-c7c8-555f-8bf6-a84746d0aacb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237773 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237773 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237773 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236501 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237773 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186236631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237773 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186237317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237773 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237773 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237773 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186236258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237773 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fe30c037-d401-593e-a43e-6b8a2fcfc035" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237950 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186237773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237950 #edb/ref 1069 "q-102802" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237950 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237950 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y=4 \\\\ 6=5x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237950 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9876e0e7-b1e4-559d-b97c-350c8c6823a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186237950 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y=4 \\\\ 5x=6.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285422 #edb/ref 1080 "images/07/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285422 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285422 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "458475cb-7c2d-5db3-9d9a-f7dcbf9640f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285585 #edb/ref 1080 "images/0f/0f219c170d7e73a8a5c3d11afabe6763e25ade77be9ed8a0b7495a8d9f6be90c.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285585 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285585 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56cc21dc-81f2-58b5-a405-76666971f42b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285592 #edb/ref 1080 "images/91/91f80f30887e5233d12ee814c1e991f81613bd52c9afd7334397b123b68b8bc7.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285592 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285592 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "57df3629-2829-5e67-a0ee-b0af9d5c5261" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285828 #edb/ref 1080 "images/6b/6bc02e0957ea0099329b8266d4960b542d86c19f44b4fc811ba0752512def666.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285828 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285828 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "71705615-b275-5206-9f46-e59b618b0dd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286912 #edb/ref 1080 "images/42/4233644fb8c5e19f379fdbc001951869fd5d9062e1f14d0abbb53d677780fb0a.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286912 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286912 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e7ebacdf-8af4-5d1c-ad4f-a5eaba6a49e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287435 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287435 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287435 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287435 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287435 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287435 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287435 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287435 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186285422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287435 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "88fca9fa-b9b5-5967-9c21-b7010d8c4956" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287751 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287751 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181775" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287751 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287751 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=R\\times R$ in the Cartesian plane?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287751 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1e98098c-88d7-594b-ad3c-687cf15456dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287751 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set\n\n$$\nS=R\\times R\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in R,\\,y\\in R}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{0}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $0$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{0}={(0,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{0}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/07/07a3d9a6c38b5bfcc529496735a1a66eaceefd5ae3437a2cb0cd45911eccafae.png)\n\nNow, consider a general ${S}_{i}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals some $i\\in R$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any real number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{i}={(i,y)\\,:\\,y\\in R}\n$$\n\nFor each $i\\in R,$ ${S}_{i}$ is a vertical line.\n\n![](images/e4/e454f1cf125486ca25acf15e26efd251a4a03b08e899814ab3e77db7898713c4.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product $S$ is the union of these subsets over $R:$\n\n$$\nS={⋃}_{i\\in R}{S}_{i}.\n$$\n\nThis is the whole plane, as shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/07/070389fcdb6d69f9aa90dabbd98a0d3461e26d3e3e08b1d53b92e99688c09923.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390402 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186390403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390402 #edb/ref 1069 "q-21058" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390402 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390402 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fe/fee79ec0b214a4ba87400b4b8c9dab2c623878d067821c572b26ae241625c48a.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390402 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f7e170ff-3ef3-51ef-bb76-d32ad791f4a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390402 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 15 & 25\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(2,10)$, $(3,15)$, and  $(5,25).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](images/bf/bf5987fde11416780a6a599e3952db7319e1c0e859e2439b7df70c5659bc6839.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390403 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390403 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390403 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390403 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390403 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186390408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390403 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390403 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390403 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186390405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390403 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8cfcca37-0c5f-5e1f-94b7-02dbf414d41e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390404 #edb/ref 1080 "images/e6/e667849ed8a214e7d17871b0f96f73f83c59eec2677bfbaeaab589e04cc89e61.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390404 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390404 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cd55c037-00e6-5219-914e-9a5a9bd7534e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390405 #edb/ref 1080 "images/52/52266ff97300b29c85ac14f5b60b308d9e8a0e2fe3a01e8e0431b643e6a28922.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390405 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390405 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f174cb91-e1ee-5d6c-90ef-6029cbaebf29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390406 #edb/ref 1080 "images/1a/1a027e19617c0c62fd8f5247c6d1bbac894f9522ec9e90aec5b7ed05b3996b37.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390406 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186390406 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "071cdea1-0dac-5f25-b6f4-63481ba1e33c" #